eError","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"RELEASE","status":"SUCCESS","tag":"v1.1.3.2.10"},"18":{"id":18,"sha":"b03c90b64edf8cb8a92f1fd729110f16d7ce4ae5","date":"17 Jul 2026 (16:55:35)","timestamp":20260717165535,"message":"fix(1.8): isolate BlockDropItemEvent and EntityPickupItemEvent handlers","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"RELEASE","status":"SUCCESS","tag":"v1.1.3.2.11"},"19":{"id":19,"sha":"5ce70cbd342c2b3f44bbef21e8fa12c325d44dc4","date":"18 Jul 2026 (08:36:35)","timestamp":20260718083635,"message":"fix(1.8): resolve TileState reflectively to stop NoClassDefFoundError on every block break\n\norg.bukkit.block.TileState is a 1.14+ class; referencing it directly in\nisValidBreakEvent crashed BlockBreakListener on 1.8.8 for every block break.\nNow resolved via Class.forName, short-circuiting to false when absent.","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"RELEASE","status":"SUCCESS","tag":"v1.1.3.2.12"},"20":{"id":20,"sha":"903a5dc56af6901ba1bd91b977634ff1c93cff3e","date":"22 Jul 2026 (11:48:14)","timestamp":20260722114814,"message":"feat(guide): declare categories, drop custom guide UI, surface item groups","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"RELEASE","status":"SUCCESS","tag":"v1.1.3.2.13"},"21":{"id":21,"sha":"e35337205aa760f5db92355e7a0eaddc7d613d74","date":"06 Aug 2026 (12:55:49)","timestamp":20260806125549,"message":"feat(i18n): translate tinker tools/armour/parts via ItemTextResolver, retire re-skin listener\n\nAssembled tinker items are named+lored from their PDC at runtime; they now route through core's\nper-viewer packet layer via an item-aware resolver (which overrides their static guide-id entry only\nfor assembled instances) instead of the bespoke TinkerTranslationListener inventory re-skin. Removes\nTinkerTranslationListener + TinkerPickupListener; bumps sfCoreVersion to gh-v5.3.2.3 for the resolver\nprecedence change.","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"22":{"id":22,"sha":"0dde6c25f54b387d8753be3cb65e7772813d8f84","date":"07 Aug 2026 (00:20:56)","timestamp":20260807002056,"message":"style(comments): remove redundant and self-explanatory comments","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"23":{"id":23,"sha":"ef5e1793bb159d4e77d53a69b253a69ca37cd7ef","date":"10 Aug 2026 (15:58:40)","timestamp":20260810155840,"message":"refactor(slimetinker): extract newTraitKeySafeYaml and move compat rationale into javadoc","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"24":{"id":24,"sha":"f5954d28f4330010e1774f14c57660a20d02db65","date":"14 Aug 2026 (21:59:46)","timestamp":20260814215946,"message":"fix(guide): defer guide-type categorisation until the item registry finalizes\n\nItemGroups#categorise() iterated group.getItems() directly from\nonEnable(), but core only links a SlimefunItem into its ItemGroup via\nload(), which runs for every item on the first tick after all addons\nenable. Every group was still empty at that point, so no item ever\ngot a declared guide type and everything fell back to Misc (or an\nunrelated heuristic match). Run categorise() from a listener on\nSlimefunItemRegistryFinalizedEvent instead, fired right after that\nloop completes.","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"25":{"id":25,"sha":"2c52074194e714b62f57c4547946d71e0877385c","date":"15 Aug 2026 (13:17:05)","timestamp":20260815131705,"message":"feat(smeltery): auto-build the seared structure around a placed controller\n\nPlacing the smeltery controller (by hand or cheated) only ever placed that\none block, leaving the player to hand-place all 6 seared bricks, the tank\nand the spout - unlike a core multiblock, whose place-to-build assembler\nbuilds its whole structure from a single placement. The smeltery was never\na core MultiBlockMachine (it validates its structure by counting BlockStorage\nids around the controller on menu-open, in TinkersSmeltery), so that\nassembler never ran for it.\n\nHooks the same core-side generic assembler (MultiBlockAssembler.assembleAround)\nonto the controller's placement instead, at MONITOR priority so it only runs\nonce the controller's own placement/permission checks already passed. Builds\nthe exact block counts TinkersSmeltery#validateMultiblock already expects.","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"FAILURE"},"26":{"id":26,"sha":"d810b9259f41e0378ff739fa9fd4eacaf1a21f41","date":"15 Aug 2026 (18:24:25)","timestamp":20260815182425,"message":"chore(deps): bump core dependency to released tag 5.3.2.5","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"FAILURE"},"27":{"id":27,"sha":"ab825e6c007aa74bbb3c00e6f4b0cba2779d9d80","date":"15 Aug 2026 (19:11:08)","timestamp":20260815191108,"message":"fix(items): guard against a null lore list in themedItemStack\n\nSlimefun core no longer bakes a placeholder lore line onto fresh item\ntemplates, so ItemMeta.getLore() now returns null instead of an empty\nlist. themedItemStack crashed with an NPE on the first call, which\nhappened during Parts's static initializer and aborted onEnable before\nregisterTranslations ran, leaving all 139 items untranslated.","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"28":{"id":28,"sha":"52beeac558871e2f4e7fcc1af862d25114cf0d27","date":"17 Aug 2026 (19:21:19)","timestamp":20260817192119,"message":"fix(smeltery): build the seared structure from the guide multiblock item","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"29":{"id":29,"sha":"e2ddb7c4cb49eb09c2e3d62f912ed9a7e86114a7","date":"17 Aug 2026 (20:05:51)","timestamp":20260817200551,"message":"fix(smeltery): register the controller directly when assembling the multiblock","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"30":{"id":30,"sha":"018dd6077d33c1bcaff27ec9a4397e5281f05f28","date":"17 Aug 2026 (21:41:01)","timestamp":20260817214101,"message":"refactor(smeltery): let the assembler place the controller cell","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"RELEASE","status":"SUCCESS","tag":"v1.1.3.2.14"},"31":{"id":31,"sha":"c8e05e8e1acfae44b661d542c754f1ac509781ed","date":"20 Aug 2026 (08:40:04)","timestamp":20260820084004,"message":"ci(workflows): regenerate the readme after promotion and follow the ci rename","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-3.0","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Slimefun5/SlimeTinker/stable/LICENSE"},"candidate":"DEVELOPMENT","status":"SUCCESS"},"32":{"id":32,"sha":"694d901d227690ab00163a76361c432ea20608d6","date":"20 Aug 2026 (10:23:32)","timestamp":20260820102332,"message":"ci(workflows): allow the workflows to be run by hand","author":"intisy (Finn Birich)","avatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105643708?v=4","license":{"name":"GNU General Public License v3.0","id":"GPL-